  "name": "Making a Brew",
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": true,
      "text": "[#](53341a)A brew is an ordered chain of no more than **eight physical ingredients**. Drop ordinary reagents into the hot bowl one at a time. Each accepted item is consumed and the water takes its colour.[#]()",
      "title": "Making a Brew",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": false,
      "text": "[#](53341a)Some dual-purpose ingredients must be **sneak-stirred** by using them directly on the cauldron. This keeps them from being swallowed while the cauldron is waiting for an old crafting recipe. The reference pages mark every such ingredient.[#]()",
      "title": " ",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": true,
      "text": "[#](53341a)Capacity must be opened before an effect or world action can fit. Strength, duration, inversion, particle, and target modifiers shape the **next** accepted effect or action, then their temporary state resets.[#]() [#](53341a)A rejected ingredient remains yours.[#]()",
      "title": "Order Matters",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": false,
      "text": "[#](53341a)If the bowl refuses an effect, add enough capacity first; if it refuses everything, the eight-item batch is already full or a final ritual target has closed the recipe.[#]()",
      "title": " ",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
